## Working rules
1. Continue from this checkpoint; do not start again.
2. Locked phases stay closed unless a later integration exposes a specific defect.
3. Use the smallest necessary inspection/check before changing code.
4. Avoid broad/repetitive debugging.
5. Workflow: targeted test/check → exact diagnosis → smallest correct change → rerun targeted test → logical checkpoint → full suite only at a lock/cross-stack checkpoint.
6. Do not invent API fields, enum values, components, GPIO pins, relay polarity, ADC channels, timings, thresholds, or wiring.
7. Current hardware/components are not finalized; unknown values remain unresolved.
8. Laptop-first development must work with simulated/test persisted data.
9. Physical Raspberry Pi behavior stays behind the HAL/runtime boundary.
10. Never infer physical execution from a DB default/configuration alone.
11. Prefer complete-file replacements when partial edits are error-prone.
12. Preserve known-good code and tests.
13. Use Windows PowerShell.
14. Do not run Pi/Linux `.sh` scripts on Windows.
15. Do not rerun the full backend suite for frontend-only changes.
16. Ignore the Vitest repeated-jsdom performance note unless there is an actual test problem.

